 "summary": "The iOS side of WP2 is done. The earlier run's WIP commit already built cleanly with all 693 tests green, and it covered nearly every item in the binding contract and the iOS design. Auditing it item by item turned up no missing design items, so my work was verifying it on the simulator and fixing what that exposed. All changes are uncommitted on top of HEAD d069d2b; I did not edit android/ or any shared files.\n\nAlready in the WIP and checked against the design:\n- **Tile view:** CALayer compositor with a pure draw planner. Tiles sit on exact float frames from one grid origin, with no inflation or rounding (D4-16). Parent/child fallback works for every raster source, the cache is a memory-only byte LRU sized by RAM, decoding is off the main thread, and the camera is clamped to 2...22 with an underzoom guard and unwrapped columns at the antimeridian.\n- **PDF tiles:** footprint, clip and zoom policy, the adaptive warp planner, the renderer (base raster / direct vector / staged), the lane scheduler, PDFTileSource, PDFMapRuntime and the crash-loop guard. The old single-image overlay (PDFOverlay, PDFTiler and the PDFMapSource image cache) is gone.\n- **Bake:** PDFBakeController and PDFBakeWorker. Writes go to pdf_bake_work/*.partial, protection is completeUntilFirstUserAuthentication, the PDF is kept, and the bake is cancellable, shows progress, estimates size/time and survives sheet dismissal.\n- **Rest:** the `importedMapVisible` toggle, render failures shown in the header label/alert/Layers row, the import probe, latest-wins cancellation of MGRS grid builds, the DEBUG-only launch hooks, docs/DEBUG_HOOKS.md and the THREAT_MODEL.md \u00a79 note.\n\nFixed this session:\n1. **SwiftUI warning:** \"Publishing changes from within view updates\" fired on every PDF launch, because building the tile source inside `updateUIView` published its render status. `syncSource` now defers the PDF source creation by one runloop turn, and only applies it if nothing newer arrived. The warning no longer appears in the device logs.\n2. **Restored map invisible on cold launch:** at launch the saved map was framed before the map view had a size, so the fit landed near z4 and the sheet was one dark pixel under the crosshair. `flyTo` now fits against the screen height until the view is laid out. Confirmed on device with before/after screenshots. This bug predates WP2.\n3. **Stale comment** in WebMercatorTiles that still mentioned PDFTiler.\n\nNew tests: an exact-float-frame test for D4-16 and a regression test for the cold-launch framing.",
