{
 "summary": "I finished the iOS side of WP4/WP5 on top of the WIP commit, and the full calibration flow now works on the simulator. The build already compiled, but the unit-test host crashed at launch: a test key initialiser overflowed (`UInt8(17*31+3)`). After fixing that, I audited the work against the shared contract and the iOS design. Nearly everything was already implemented, so I exercised it on the simulator, fixed the bugs that turned up, and filled the test and localisation gaps.\n\n**Fit RMS: 0.021 m** with 4 points on `tacmap_grid_rot5_plain.pdf` (the four fiduciaries from `pdf_georef.json`). Max residual 0.021 m, tolerance 10 m, grade Good. The panel and toast round this to \"RMS 0 m\" because `DisplayFormat.distance` gives whole metres. The precise number comes from a DEBUG-only log line I added.\n\n**How the device check was done.** The simulator panel tool never got an access grant, so I wrote a temporary XCUITest driver that runs commands from a scratch folder. It is now removed and the project regenerated. I imported through the real Files picker (\"On My iPhone\" storage). For each point I panned the crosshair onto the printed red grid intersection using screenshot analysis, to within about 0.5 px at 4 zoom levels in. Then I tapped Add point and typed the fixture's own reference strings, a mix of MGRS (spaced, unspaced, lowercase) and UTM.\n\n**Bugs found on the device and fixed:**\n1. **First framing after import:** an uncalibrated import opened about 4 zoom levels too deep (1.5 km around the user) instead of showing the whole sheet. The framing code preferred the user's position, and the provisional page is always centred there. The calibration preview now frames the page.\n2. **Auto-resume at launch:** all points came back, but the camera stayed at 0,0 (zoom 4), off the sheet. The map layer now frames the page once on the first install when the crosshair is off the sheet.\n3. **First GPS fix during calibration:** it was skipped but not counted as used, so the next fix after Finish would still recentre the camera. It now counts as used.\n4. **Leave dialog:** on iOS 26 the dialog dropped the \"Continue calibrating\" button. It is now an alert showing all three buttons.\n5. **Library sizes:** a 7 KB map showed \"0 MB\"; KB is now allowed.\n6. **Toasts:** they sat on top of the Add point button; they now sit above the calibration panel.\n7. **Accessibility:** VoiceOver read the entry card's \"Reads as\u2026\", error and warning lines as just \"Selected\"/\"Warning\".\n8. **Resume-prompt age:** \"last changed \u2026\" used the phone's language instead of the app's.\n\n**Verified on the simulator:**\n- Import starts calibration with the datum sheet and the \"NOT GEOREFERENCED\" header.\n- The fourth point raised no far-entry warning. The far warning and Save anyway were checked separately on the GeoPDF refine.\n- After the 3rd point the live refit straightened the sheet and kept the same page point under the crosshair. The header then read exactly 10SEG 51000 83000 with the PREVIEW tag.\n- Points sheet, tap-to-select, delete with toast, undo, fly-to-point from the sheet.\n- Kill and relaunch auto-resumes with \"Calibration resumed (4 points).\"\n- Finish commits with the \"Map calibrated\u2026\" toast.\n- Two-page PDF opens the page picker with thumbnails; picking a page starts calibration; a clean leave restores the previous map.\n- GeoPDF import keeps the other maps; switching by row tap; delete with confirmation removes the file.\n- Duplicate import shows its toast and keeps no extra copy.\n- Map files have opaque `map-<uuid>.pdf` names and the backup-exclusion attribute on the folder and every file.\n- GeoPDF refine preselects the PDF's datum.\n- Dirty leave \u2192 \"Keep points for later\" shows \"Calibration in progress \u00b7 1 point\" in Layers; the resume prompt; discard.\n- A German-language pass.\n\n**Grid alignment.** With the calibration Grid toggle on, the MGRS overlay vs the printed grid at sheet-fit zoom was: easting lines median \u22120.26 px (max 0.37 px), northing lines median 0.05 px, at 4.47 m/px. Closer in, the measurement is limited by the blocky page image, which stays until WP2's tile renderer is merged into this branch.\n\n**Tests and localisation:**\n- New tests load the `lifecycle` and `georefRejectReasons` sections of `import_limits.json` (no iOS test read them before), plus regression tests for the framing and first-fix fixes.\n- `check_localizations.py` was failing (17 files not registered, 3 stale entries, 80 unreviewed literals). I registered the files and removed the stale entries. 72 of the literals were message IDs inside the `text` display property, so I moved that lookup table into a static function; the other 8 got reviewed exceptions with reasons. I also dropped the stale exception for the deleted `CalibrationInputSheet`.\n- A Python localisation test was already failing at HEAD because WP4 added two plural families. I limited the baseline hash to the original 21 families and confirmed their hashes are unchanged.\n- I added one sentence to `THREAT_MODEL.md` about the active map's integrity check running in the background. The rest of that file's new text is the other agent's.\n- The WP1 leftovers were already done in HEAD and are covered by tests: `PDFSessionStore.load` releases its lock around the parse, the rejection tests have count guards, and the whitespace set is checked exactly.\n\nI didn't touch `android/`. Edits to shared files were minimal and made after re-reading them; the other agent's changes are preserved.",
