 "test_results": "Full iOS unit suite (`-only-testing:TacticalMapsTests` on sim 6752680A): 663 tests run, 0 failures, 1 skipped (`SyncProtocolV3Tests.testLiveProductionHandshakeWhenRelayIsProvided`, needs a live relay). The 14 new tests all pass.\n\nHow the count moved:\n- 617 before these packages.\n- HEAD's WIP commit has 649. At the start of this session the suite didn't run at all: the test host crashed at launch on a `UInt8` overflow in the `ImportedMapLibraryTests` key, which I fixed.\n- 663 now.\n\nThe WIP commit had removed 17 tests, all pinning behaviour the plan replaces:\n- 14 in `ActiveMapSelectionStoreTests`, built on the single retained map and the selection commit coordinator. Their replacements are the library tests in `ImportedMapLibraryTests`.\n- 3 in `CalibrationSessionTests`, for the old tap-to-place fiduciary session. They were replaced by the crosshair-session tests.\n\nI removed no tests myself.\n\nLocalisation:\n- `python3 scripts/check_localizations.py`: PASS (\"Display guard: 391 source components, 61 reviewed literal occurrences. Validated 2088 messages, 23 plural families, translation review fingerprints and all native outputs.\").\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts -p 'test_localization*.py'`: 31 tests OK. One of these was already failing at HEAD, fixed as described in the summary.",
 "device_checks": "iOS Simulator 6752680A (\"TacMap Review iPhone 2\", iOS 26.5), clean install with the keychain reset. Driven through a temporary XCUITest command driver (since removed); file imports went through the real document picker \u2192 Browse \u2192 On My iPhone. Screenshots: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-cbrooker-Code-TacticalMaps/d9f42208-9d3f-40e1-9b8b-49fa6c488260/scratchpad/wp4-shots/ios/ (29 PNGs: run1-* before the fixes, run2-*/run3-* after).\n\n**Calibration of `tacmap_grid_rot5_plain.pdf`, WGS84, the 4 grid-intersection fiduciaries:**\n- Each point was placed by aligning the crosshair to the printed red grid intersection to within about 0.1\u20130.5 px at 4 zoom levels in (about 0.2 m). Inputs: `10SEG4700077000`, `10S EG 51000 77000`, `10seg 51000 83000`, `10S 547000 4183000`.\n- Panel: \"4 points \u00b7 RMS 0 m \u00b7 Good\". Log: rms=0.021 m, max=0.021 m, tolerance 10.0 m. Finish toast: \"Map calibrated \u00b7 4 points \u00b7 RMS 0 m\".\n- After the 3rd point the live refit kept the intersection under the crosshair (602.9, 1310.5 px vs the reticle at 603, 1311). Grid slopes went from \u00b10.087 (the sheet's 5\u00b0 skew) to the expected UTM grid convergence of about 0.0058.\n- Calibration Grid toggle, overlay vs printed grid at sheet-fit zoom (4.47 m/px): easting median \u22120.26 px (max 0.37 px), northing median 0.05 px. At 2 zoom levels in, the median on the line through the crosshair is 0.54 px (0.6 m).\n- At 4 zoom levels in, the blocky low-resolution page image limits the measurement. That's WP2's renderer, not merged here.\n- After Finish, the normal map display measured within about 1.1 px at 4.8 m/px (run 1).\n\n**Lifecycle checks:** run1-16 shows the old 2-button leave dialog before the fix; run3-01 shows the fixed 3-button alert.\n- Auto-resume after a kill: run 1 hit the 0,0 camera bug; run 2, after the fix, frames the sheet with all 4 markers and the \"Calibration resumed (4 points).\" toast.\n- Two-page plain PDF opens the page picker with thumbnails. Picking page 2 starts calibration; a clean leave restores the previous map without reframing.\n- Imported a GeoPDF: 3 maps listed with correct states. Delete showed the confirmation and removed the file; row tap switched maps.\n- Duplicate re-import shows the toast and keeps no extra file.\n- Backup-exclusion attribute present on ImportedMaps and on every `map-<uuid>.pdf`.\n- GeoPDF \"Calibrate / refine\u2026\": no datum sheet (WGS84 from the PDF), live coordinates, no PREVIEW tag. Far-entry warning \"1.41 km\u2026\" with Save anyway.\n- Dirty leave \u2192 Keep gives the Layers subtitle \"Calibration in progress \u00b7 1 point\". The resume prompt read \"\u20261 point, last changed 37 seconds ago.\"; Resume, then leave \u2192 Discard removes the draft.\n- German pass (app language set to `de`): Layers library row, panel, points sheet, datum sheet and header \"Kalibrierung l\u00e4uft\" all in German.",
