 "summary": "Android WP4/WP5 is finished on top of the WIP commit; all changes are uncommitted in /Users/cbrooker/Code/TacticalMaps/.claude/worktrees/review-wp4.\n\nStarting point: the WIP already compiled and its suite was green (735 tests, 0 failures, 1 skipped). Most of the design was in place: the controller, panel, entry card, the points and datum sheets, markers, reticle, the atomic georef/camera swap, the sealed library and drafts, the migration, the pipeline and inspector, page picker, progress card and imported-maps section.\n\nWhat was missing or wrong, and is now fixed:\n1. **D5-18 not done.** The picked URI was still written to plaintext prefs. It now lives in memory and savedInstanceState only. The old pending_document_import_v1 file is read once, adopted and wiped, and leftover read grants are released at startup.\n2. **No pure library reducer.** Added LibraryReducer (same cases and rules as iOS) and routed every library transition in MapViewModel through it.\n3. **Choose page did nothing.** The menu item only showed a toast. It now re-reads the entry's own file under the 30 s watchdog with progress and Cancel, opens the page picker, and applies the change in one library write that drops the calibration and the old page's draft. It asks first (map_change_page_confirm) when the map has a hand calibration. \"Use the PDF's own georeferencing\" now confirms too.\n4. **D5-15 boundary.** The MapScreen import job caught Throwable; it now catches Exception only, so OOM/StackOverflow are handled solely at the inspector. The inspector now maps every PDFBox failure to a typed error (scratch cap = tooComplex, other junk = invalidPdf).\n5. **Launch-time toasts were lost.** Calibration events were a SharedFlow with no subscriber at VM init, so the auto-resume toast never appeared. They are now a buffered Channel.\n6. **Extended pdf_georef.json rejections.** The Android reader hid pdf null values and accepted Kotlin-only number strings (10d, 10f, hex, NaN). It now keeps a null as present-with-the-wrong-type on georef keys, gates number strings on the shared grammar (new PdfValueRules), trims text with the shared whitespace set, and treats a junk StandardParallelTwo as malformed instead of defaulting it. All 34 valueTypeCases pass on the JVM and through PDFBox on device; all 10 pageBudgetCases pass.\n7. **Device-found UX fixes.** The entry field now takes focus and raises the keyboard when the card opens. The panel's action row is disabled while the card is open (tapping Add point there silently discarded the typed entry). Tapping a marker now flies to it, as the contract requires.\n8. **Instrumented tests that no longer compiled.** PdfImportHardeningInstrumentedTest and PdfImportSmokeTest still called the removed preflight/importPdfMapSource API; I ported them to the new pipeline.\n9. **Localization and docs.** Registered the 28 new Android sources in the inventory and removed 2 stale Android exceptions. Updated docs/THREAT_MODEL.md: imported map files are now an untrusted boundary, the at-rest paragraph describes the sealed library and opaque names, and there is a new paragraph on untrusted-PDF parsing limits.\n\nWP1 leftovers: saveToLibrary already runs its load-modify-commit under SESSION_LOCK. The equivalent of the restoreActiveMapSource Missing branch (now LegacyMapReader) already checks legacyPdfMigrationPending(). Every Android L10n.text literal already has a catalogue entry with German, so nothing was left to move.\n\nOn-device fit for tacmap_grid_rot5_plain.pdf with its 4 grid-intersection fiduciaries: n=4, RMS 0.192 m, max residual 0.192 m, tolerance 10 m, grade Good. Device details are under device_checks.",
