 "test_results": "- **Android unit suite (final run):** 791 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, 1 skipped. Baseline was 735 at the WIP HEAD (726 before these packages), so 56 new tests.\n- **assembleDebug:** BUILD SUCCESSFUL.\n- **Instrumented, emulator-5564** (selected classes only, not the whole connected suite):\n  - GeoPdfFixtureInstrumentedTest + PdfImportHardeningInstrumentedTest: 24 pass, 1 skipped (the USGS sample isn't on the device).\n  - PdfImportSmokeTest, MBTilesLifecycleInstrumentedTest, PdfSessionMigrationInstrumentedTest, PdfRendererConventionInstrumentedTest, LocalizationTest: 28 pass. This includes the real-picker UI test.\n  - LocalizationTest re-run after adding the plural test: 13/13 pass.\n- **Tests updated because the plan replaced what they pinned:**\n  - Done by the earlier WIP: deleted ImportedMapGeoreferencingTest (pinned the old fiduciary status helpers); removed the MapScreenParityTest GPS-to-MGRS fiduciary case; PdfImportPreflightContractTest now expects the shared typed messages and the 512 MiB limit instead of the old 256 MB text.\n  - Done by me: PdfImportHardeningInstrumentedTest moved from preflightPdfImport to PdfInspector typed errors. PdfImportSmokeTest moved to the new pipeline; a single-page refused GeoPDF is now added as rejected, and the UI test expects the datum sheet, NOT GEOREFERENCED and the X leave button.\n- **check_localizations.py:** exit 1 with 101 findings, none of them Android. All are iOS-owned: inventory rows for new/deleted iOS Swift files, message-key literals in iOS CalibrationMessageText.swift and others, and stale exception 32ca0e33edd5347f for the deleted iOS CalibrationInputSheet.swift. I did not touch ios/; the iOS agent has to clear these before the script passes.",
 "device_checks": "Emulator-5564 (API 36, 1080x2400), debug build, real picker. Screenshots in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-cbrooker-Code-TacticalMaps/d9f42208-9d3f-40e1-9b8b-49fa6c488260/scratchpad/wp4-shots/android/ (00 to 39).\n\n**Import (DocumentsUI, file pushed to /sdcard/Download)**\n- Import / Export > PDF Map > tacmap_grid_rot5_plain.pdf goes straight into calibration with the datum sheet first, full datum list in contract order.\n- shared_prefs has no URI or file name.\n- The copy is pdf_maps/import-<16hex>.pdf and the library file is sealed.\n\n**Calibration screen**\n- The page is framed on the provisional placement.\n- Header shows NOT GEOREFERENCED with an amber \"Calibrating\" label; distance, elevation and grid-magnetic are hidden.\n- The calibration reticle is shown, the chrome is hidden, and the \u2715, zoom \u00b1 and panel buttons are present.\n\n**Placing the four fiduciaries**\n- Placed with pan and zoom only (exact `input motionevent` pans plus a script that fits the printed red grid lines).\n- Reticle-to-intersection residual at placement was \u22640.48 px at zoom +3 (about 0.06 pt).\n- References typed exactly as the fixture writes them: 10SEG4700077000, 10S EG 51000 77000, 10seg 51000 83000, 10S 547000 4183000. The live \"Reads as\" line was right for each (the last one read as UTM, with S as a band, not south).\n- Each point got the marker \"+\" with an up-right badge, the next-corner hint, and a draft written synchronously.\n\n**Fit**\n- At 3 points the display swapped to the fit with the page point held under the reticle. The header then read 10SEG 51000 82999 with the PREVIEW tag, and the exact-fit warning showed.\n- With the reticle on the printed F4 intersection, the header read exactly 10SEG 47000 83000 before point 4 was added.\n- After 4 points: \"4 points \u00b7 RMS 0 m \u00b7 Good\"; the Points sheet shows every residual as 0 m with a check.\n- Debug commit log: **n=4, RMS 0.192 m, max 0.192 m, \u03c4 10 m, grade good.**\n\n**Grid overlay vs printed grid (grid_alignment.py, reticle masked)**\n- Median offset 0.03\u20130.09 px at base zoom (about 8 m/px) and 0.01\u20130.03 px at z+1 (about 4 m/px).\n- Max values are 0.7\u20133 px; the remaining outliers come from marker crosses and the location dot that the script counts as overlay grey.\n\n**Finish and persistence**\n- Toast \"Map calibrated \u00b7 4 points \u00b7 RMS 0 m\"; the camera didn't move; normal chrome came back.\n- A relaunch restores the calibrated PDF as the basemap. Layers shows \"Calibrated \u00b7 4 points \u00b7 RMS 0 m\", the size, the overflow menu and the footer.\n\n**Refine, kill and resume**\n- Calibrate / refine\u2026 from the row menu seeds the 4 saved points.\n- The field auto-focused. The 8-figure shorthand 50007900 completed from the map (\"Zone and square from the map\", 10 m cell), giving 5 points at RMS 0 m.\n- Force-stop then relaunch: auto-resume with the toast \"Calibration resumed (5 points).\" and the PREVIEW tag.\n- \u2715 showed the Keep / Discard / Continue dialog. \"Keep points for later\" left the row reading \"Calibration in progress \u00b7 5 points\".\n\n**Library and delete**\n- A second import (the GeoPDF variant) went straight to active; the library holds both maps (2 maps \u00b7 15 kB).\n- Delete\u2026 showed the confirm dialog, and the file stayed until I confirmed.\n- After deleting: the plain PDF is gone from pdf_maps, its draft is gone (sealed drafts file back to empty), and the other map is untouched.\n\nThe pushed test PDFs were removed from Downloads. The app is uninstalled now because the last connected-test run removes it.",
